ence; do NOT reap unless ahead>0+clean+content-identical.","acceptance":"test -f .env.example exits 0, and the loop `for v in $(grep -rhoE 'process\\.env\\.[A-Z_0-9]+' src bin scripts | sed 's/process\\.env\\.//' | sort -u); do grep -q \"^$v=\" .env.example || echo MISSING $v; done` prints no MISSING lines, i.e. every environment variable name the code reads has an entry in .env.example.","worktree":null,"branch":null,"sessions":null,"worker_status":"pending","dispatched_at":null}
 {"status":"complete","id":"DOC-3","title":"operator path: document daemon lifecycle, port, pid/log location, orphan + corrupt-db recovery","detail":{"fingerprint":"462d6fea38be5b1a9d3713f02aec94305d4ddebc57e65db368cde1ecbaaf30c7","evidence":[{"run_id":"e5448b3b","ts":"2026-11-17T10:45:45.198514+00:00","tree_fp":"1c174816e82ba68e590c79d03b1a062b54af8ff32a79994e24784c9e8f05a2d5","artifacts":["/home/kara/.hermes/cache/scratch/speclang-readme-1117-1010/doc3_check.py"]}]},"priority":"P4","source":null,"reasoning":"Operator path gap (3am reader). Command run: ./bin/speclang status -> prints \"Daemon: Not running\" when the daemon is down and nothing else; neither docs/troubleshooting.md nor README tells an operator how to reach that state on purpose or what the recovery ladder is. No operator runbook exists in the repo (ls docs/ -> API_REFERENCE, BOOTSTRAP_PLAN, CASCADE_DEMO, CHANGELOG, CONTEXT, COORDINATOR, DOGFOODING, MASTER_GUIDE, NORTH_STAR, PRD.html, PY_SPEC_CONCEPT, layers.md, prompts/, troubleshooting.md, user-flows.md + archive/ + dogfood/; no runbook/OPERATIONS file).\nLive evidence for what the runbook must cover:\n- port: `speclang start --help` -> \"-p, --port <port>  Dashboard port (default: \"3000\")\"; 3000 collides with other local services and the flag appears in no doc (grep -rn \"\\-\\-port\" README.md GETTING-STARTED.md PACKAGING.md -> only PACKAGING.md mentions a port in passing). Pending QA row DF-SPECLANG-5 already names port collision for the RUNTIME side; this row is the operator DOC (how to change it).\n- PID/lifecycle: `speclang daemon --help` -> start/stop/status; `speclang stop` docs absent; the daemon's pid/log location is documented nowhere (MCP_LOG_FILE exists but is undocumented - see the env-var row).\n- stale/leftover daemons: a leaked `speclangd start --config=.speclangrc` child was observed reparented to systemd --user running hours after its parent test suite exited (see the foreman's own incident notes) - an operator has no doc telling them to `ps -o pid,ppid,etime,cmd` and kill it.\n- corrupted state: `.speclang/speclang.db` corruption is silently tolerated (pending QA-SPECLANG-5: build/status exit 0 on a truncated db) - the runbook must state the current (missing) integrity check and the safe reset procedure (delete .speclang/speclang.db and let the daemon rebuild).\nARTIFACT: docs/OPERATIONS.md (new) OR a \"Running SpecLang\" section in docs/troubleshooting.md.\nREADER: operator.\nACCEPT: an operator with no chat history can, from the repo root, find: how to start/stop/status the daemon, how to change the dashboard port, where the daemon writes its pid + log, how to find and kill an orphaned speclangd, and what to do when .speclang/speclang.db is corrupt - each with the exact command and its expected output.","ts":null,"complexity":3,"created_at":"2026-09-27T01:15:30.546264+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-17T10:45:45.198514+00:00","acceptance":"At least one non-archive doc under docs/ carries the full daemon operator path: python3 -c \"import glob;oks=[f for f in glob.glob('docs/*.md') if all(s in open(f).read() for s in ('daemon.pid','daemon.log','3000'))];print('OK' if oks else 'FAIL');print(oks)\" prints OK and lists a file, and the same lookup restricted to the three daemon subcommands also returns a file: python3 -c \"import glob;need=['speclang daemon start','speclang daemon stop','speclang daemon status'];good=[f for f in glob.glob('docs/*.md') if all(s in open(f).read() for s in ('daemon.pid','daemon.log','3000')) and all(n in open(f).read() for n in need)];print('OK' if good else 'FAIL');print(good)\" prints OK with a non-empty file list. Values are the verified source defaults: port 3000 (src/daemon/daemon-cli.ts:40), pid .speclang/daemon.pid (daemon-cli.ts:47), log .speclang/daemon.log (src/daemon/config.ts:35).","foreman_note":"Doc-severity re-triage 2026-10-27 per Bane ruling 2026-09-30 (documentation findings are P4, P5 for polish \u2014 never P1-P3): priority P2 -> P4. This is a POLICY change, not a new assessment; the finding is unchanged and re-verified this tick.\n\nRe-verified live: `./bin/speclang start --help` prints \"-p, --port <port>  Dashboard port (default: \\\"3000\\\")\" and `./bin/speclang status` prints only \"Daemon: Not running\" when down; no non-archive doc under docs/ carries daemon.pid / daemon.log / port 3000 (grep of docs/*.md), so the operator path is still undocumented.\n\nLeft at P4 rather than lower because a reader who needs the runbook has no pointer at all; not raised above P4 because the daemon commands the README names DO run (this is missing documentation, not a documented path that is broken \u2014 the P1 exception does not apply).\n\n2026-11-16 tick 23-53: reset from in_progress \u2014 sibling wave worker for this row died without committing any code (worktree wt/* at base, no commits; main-tree diff absent for docs rows). Shared-checkout recovery by foreman tick speclang-foreman-2026-11-16-23-53-17: sibling wave SpecLang-dogfood-2026-11-16-22-47-48 workers were killed before committing. Worktree wt/<id> kept (some have partial uncommitted edits) as salvage evidence; do NOT reap unless ahead>0+clean+content-identical.\n\nTick SpecLang-readme-2026-11-17-10-10-24. Worker wt/DOC-3 @ fab70a31; merge d6b0c471 onto origin/main pushed (0 unpushed). gitreins tier-2 verdict e5448b3b: PASS (1/1 criterion). The judge flagged one minor wording issue about .speclang/daemon-state.json being 'written by the daemon on start'; that flag is REFUTED by source: src/daemon/daemon.ts:138 calls state.setStatus(Idle) right after watcher.start()/state.load(), and specs/daemon.spec.dir/src/state.ts:91-94 persists on setStatus -> save(). No follow-up row filed. The judge also ran the full suite at HEAD: Test Files 113 passed | 4 skipped (117), Tests 1949 passed | 58 skipped (2007), with pre-existing unrelated sqlite readonly failures in tests/db.test.ts.","worktree":"/home/kara/worktrees/speclang-DOC-3","branch":"wt/DOC-3","sessions":null,"worker_status":"pending","dispatched_at":null,"commit_hash":"fab70a318980ae51fa9ee3111b44aaa3a97c8509","guard_result":"PASS","ci_result":"GREEN","worker_summary":"Daemon operator runbook landed as docs/OPERATIONS.md (symlink -> specs/docs.spec.dir/docs/OPERATIONS.md, 421 lines) following the repo dual-view convention. Both board acceptance globs run verbatim print OK ['docs/OPERATIONS.md']; port 3000 / .speclang/daemon.pid / .speclang/daemon.log verified against source; validate_refs.py prints 'All references valid.' exit 0."}
